diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index ae180e3bd..b91f69fab 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 ## [Unreleased]
 
 - Added: `fgos authority locate "<sentence>"` returns the components, decision kinds, doors and contracts that match a description of the work, and `fgos authority declare` adds or moves a model row through admission, always asking the owner before it adds a new component or decision kind; in a project with no model `locate` answers `authority: inactive` and the first `declare` creates one under `.fgos/authority/model/`. The plan contract now requires an **Authority map** (each new decision, function or module maps to a model row or to a `declare`, and a plan that overlaps something existing names the survivor), which `scripts/plan-contract-check.mjs` and the validating reviewer enforce for `draft` and `ready` plans created on or after 2026-11-24.
-- Added: `fgos doctor --fix --only <fix-id>` applies one registered fix instead of every fix, so a harness can install a workspace's agent hook rows without touching the rest.
+- Added: `fgos doctor --fix --only <fix-id>` applies one registered fix instead of every fix and judges only the rows the named fixes repair, so a harness can install a workspace's agent hook rows without touching the rest.
 - Changed: the door guard in `npm test` now matches a guarded door by primitive and by canonical name plus aliases (never by a bare word), counts matches inside allowed files, and fails a new-named copy of an owned primitive; it allows `debt` only on the named debt, 17 door rows each with a `retiredBy`, which are retired right after this release.
 - Changed: a running session cron or background task no longer blocks head session rotation (a cron never blocks and goes into the successor's handoff to recreate; a background task holds soft rotation only, rotating at hard and listing the running task in the handoff).
 - Added: a head session rotates at hard when its account's weekly quota usage reaches `sessionRotation.quota` (default 0.9) and quarantines the predecessor's account until the reported reset time; a status-line hook writer (`fgos hook session-rotation --event status-line`) captures Claude Code context and weekly rate limits beside the transcript.
